{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01BgzfihA6ScdThRoX567rDk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Claude Frontend System Design — Interview Questions\n2\t\n3\tA comprehensive reference of deep questions across all segments, organized by theme and difficulty.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## 1. Streaming & Real-Time Rendering\n8\t\n9\t> Very common. Every AI-first company asks about this.\n10\t\n11\t### Core\n12\t- How do you render incomplete Markdown mid-stream without layout thrash?\n13\t- How do you throttle token appends so the DOM doesn't repaint 50×/sec?\n14\t- How do you implement a stop-generation button that actually stops the stream?\n15\t- What is the difference between SSE and WebSockets — when would you pick each?\n16\t- How do you handle a stream that drops midway — reconnect, retry, or resume?\n17\t\n18\t### Deep\n19\t- How do you buffer tokens before flushing to the DOM — what's the right interval?\n20\t- How do you handle a code block that opens with ` ``` ` but the closing fence hasn't arrived yet?\n21\t- How do you render a streaming table where rows arrive one token at a time?\n22\t- How do you show a \"typing indicator\" that transitions seamlessly into real content?\n23\t- How do you handle backpressure if the client is rendering slower than tokens arrive?\n24\t\n25\t---\n26\t\n27\t## 2. Conversation State Management\n28\t\n29\t> Very common. Core to any chat product.\n30\t\n31\t### Core\n32\t- Where does conversation state live — client, server, or both?\n33\t- How do you handle editing a previous message and regenerating from that point?\n34\t- How do you implement branching conversations (retry gives a different response path)?\n35\t- How do you sync conversation state across two open tabs on the same conversation?\n36\t- What is your strategy when the context window fills up — truncate, summarize, or paginate?\n37\t\n38\t### Deep\n39\t- How do you model a branched conversation as a data structure — tree vs linear array?\n40\t- How do you reassemble the messages array after a mid-conversation edit?\n41\t- How do you handle optimistic UI rollback if a regenerated message fails?\n42\t- How do you implement \"undo\" for a sent message?\n43\t- How do you persist draft messages across page refreshes?\n44\t\n45\t---\n46\t\n47\t## 3. MCP & Tool Use UI\n48\t\n49\t> Emerging hot topic. Most candidates haven't thought this through.\n50\t\n51\t### Core\n52\t- How do you render a tool call pill — loading, success, and error states?\n53\t- How does a confirm button in the UI map to the backend API call?\n54\t- Why does `tool_result` go in as `role: \"user\"` in the Anthropic API?\n55\t- How do you prevent a double-booking from a confirm button being clicked twice?\n56\t- How do you communicate the trust boundary — data leaving Claude to a third-party MCP server?\n57\t\n58\t### Deep\n59\t- How do you implement idempotency keys for destructive MCP actions like bookings or emails?\n60\t- How do you render multi-step tool chains — 3 tool calls in one assistant turn?\n61\t- How do you handle a tool call that times out after 30 seconds?\n62\t- How do you diff the Anthropic vs OpenAI tool use protocol — `tool_use`/`tool_result` vs `tool_calls`/`tool` role?\n63\t- How do you handle a partial tool result — MCP server returns incomplete data?\n64\t- How do you show the user which external services were called and what data was shared?\n65\t\n66\t---\n67\t\n68\t## 4. Artifacts & Sandboxed Rendering\n69\t\n70\t> Common at companies building AI coding or document tools.\n71\t\n72\t### Core\n73\t- How do you safely render Claude-generated HTML or React in the browser?\n74\t- Why use an iframe sandbox — what attacks does it prevent?\n75\t- How do you stream code into a live-reloading preview panel?\n76\t- How does `postMessage` work between the host page and the sandboxed iframe?\n77\t- How do you version artifacts — user edits vs Claude regenerates?\n78\t\n79\t### Deep\n80\t- What CSP headers do you set on the sandboxed iframe and why?\n81\t- How do you handle an artifact that imports an external CDN library — allow or block?\n82\t- How do you diff two versions of an artifact and show a visual changelog?\n83\t- How do you sync scroll position between the code editor and the rendered preview?\n84\t- How do you handle an infinite loop inside a sandboxed React component?\n85\t- How do you implement a \"revert to version N\" for an artifact?\n86\t\n87\t---\n88\t\n89\t## 5. Performance & Scalability\n90\t\n91\t> Senior-level signal. Shows production experience.\n92\t\n93\t### Core\n94\t- How do you virtualize a conversation list with 500 messages?\n95\t- How do you measure and optimize Time to First Token (TTFT)?\n96\t- How do you lazy-load older conversation history as the user scrolls up?\n97\t- How do you avoid re-rendering the entire message list on every new token?\n98\t- How do you handle slow networks — skeleton states, progressive rendering?\n99\t\n100\t### Deep\n101\t- How do you implement scroll anchoring so new tokens don't jump the viewport?\n102\t- How do you calculate the dynamic height of a message before it has rendered (needed for virtualization)?\n103\t- How do you debounce Markdown re-parsing during a fast token stream?\n104\t- How do you measure token-per-second render rate on the client and alert on degradation?\n105\t- How do you preload the next conversation in the sidebar so it feels instant?\n106\t- What is your caching strategy for conversation history — memory, IndexedDB, server?\n107\t\n108\t---\n109\t\n110\t## 6. Auth, Security & Multitenancy\n111\t\n112\t> Senior-level. Differentiates engineers who've built multi-user systems.\n113\t\n114\t### Core\n115\t- How do you scope conversations to a user — JWT claims, row-level security?\n116\t- How do you implement org-level conversation isolation in a Team plan?\n117\t- How do you prevent prompt injection through user-uploaded files?\n118\t- How do you handle OAuth token refresh for MCP servers mid-conversation?\n119\t\n120\t### Deep\n121\t- How do you invalidate all sessions for a user on password change without breaking active streams?\n122\t- How do you implement conversation sharing with a public link — what's the permission model?\n123\t- How do you audit-log every MCP action for enterprise compliance?\n124\t- How do you prevent a malicious MCP server from exfiltrating conversation history?\n125\t- How do you scope API keys so a developer key can't access another org's conversations?\n126\t- How do you handle a user who belongs to multiple orgs — context switching mid-session?\n127\t\n128\t---\n129\t\n130\t## 7. Offline, Resilience & Error Handling\n131\t\n132\t> Differentiator. Shows you think beyond the happy path.\n133\t\n134\t### Core\n135\t- What do you show if the SSE stream disconnects at token 200 of 800?\n136\t- How do you queue a user message sent while offline and replay it on reconnect?\n137\t- How do you distinguish a rate-limit error from a model error from a network error?\n138\t- How do you implement exponential backoff on the SSE reconnect?\n139\t\n140\t### Deep\n141\t- How do you implement a \"resume stream\" — continue generation from where it dropped?\n142\t- How do you handle a partial message that was persisted to the DB mid-stream before disconnect?\n143\t- How do you show a degraded-mode UI when the inference cluster is slow (p99 > 10s)?\n144\t- What is your retry strategy for a failed MCP tool call — retry immediately, after delay, or ask user?\n145\t- How do you surface rate limit information (e.g. requests remaining) to the user without alarming them?\n146\t\n147\t---\n148\t\n149\t## 8. Input & Multimodal UX\n150\t\n151\t> Common at companies with file upload, voice, or image features.\n152\t\n153\t### Core\n154\t- How do you implement a textarea that grows with content but caps at a max height?\n155\t- How do you handle large file uploads — chunking, progress, cancellation?\n156\t- How do you render an image uploaded by the user inline in the conversation?\n157\t- How do you implement slash commands (e.g. `/search`, `/summarize`) in the input box?\n158\t\n159\t### Deep\n160\t- How do you implement voice input with live transcription feeding into the chat input?\n161\t- How do you handle a PDF upload — extract text client-side or send the raw file?\n162\t- How do you show a token count estimate for the current input before the user sends?\n163\t- How do you implement drag-and-drop file attachment with paste-from-clipboard support?\n164\t- How do you handle mixed multimodal input — image + text + file in one message?\n165\t\n166\t---\n167\t\n168\t## 9. API Design & Provider Abstraction\n169\t\n170\t> Relevant if building on top of multiple LLM providers.\n171\t\n172\t### Core\n173\t- Why does Anthropic use strict alternating turns while OpenAI allows a `tool` role?\n174\t- How do you normalize message history across Anthropic, OpenAI, and Gemini formats?\n175\t- How do you handle provider-specific features (e.g. Anthropic extended thinking) without breaking abstraction?\n176\t- What is the difference between `system` as a top-level field (Anthropic) vs a system message in the array (OpenAI)?\n177\t\n178\t### Deep\n179\t- How do you build a provider-agnostic streaming adapter — same interface for SSE and WebSocket backends?\n180\t- How do you handle model versioning — what happens when `claude-sonnet-4` is deprecated mid-product?\n181\t- How do you implement automatic model fallback if the primary model returns a 529 overloaded error?\n182\t- How do you estimate cost before sending a request — token counting per provider?\n183\t\n184\t---\n185\t\n186\t## 10. The \"Killer\" Questions\n187\t\n188\t> Questions that separate good candidates from great ones. Each forces multi-system thinking.\n189\t\n190\t1. **Edit message N in a 20-message conversation.** Forces you to think about branching history, context window re-assembly, optimistic UI rollback, and server-side state — all at once.\n191\t\n192\t2. **The confirm button is clicked twice in 200ms.** How do you guarantee exactly one booking? Covers button locking, idempotency keys, backend deduplication, and UX rollback.\n193\t\n194\t3. **The stream drops at token 400 of 1000.** What does the user see, what's in the DB, and how do you recover? Covers partial persistence, resume logic, and error UX.\n195\t\n196\t4. **Design the conversation sidebar for a user with 10,000 conversations.** Covers virtualization, search indexing, pagination, and optimistic rename/delete.\n197\t\n198\t5. **A Claude-generated React component has an infinite loop. How do you detect and handle it?** Covers sandboxing, timeout/heartbeat in the iframe, and graceful error rendering.\n199\t\n200\t6. **The MCP OAuth token expires mid-conversation during a multi-step agentic task.** Covers token refresh, mid-stream pause, user re-auth UX, and task resumption.\n201\t\n202\t---\n203\t\n204\t*Use the segmentation above to time-box your prep. Streaming + conversation state first, then MCP/artifacts, then the rest.*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f0c546b-796f-4811-b3ba-6d557f88a795","uuid":"b6a97301-2c75-4926-98ad-410f4aa0c43a","timestamp":"2026-06-20T18:24:59.452Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/claude/Claude-design-doc.md","content":"# Claude Frontend System Design — Interview Questions\n\nA comprehensive reference of deep questions across all segments, organized by theme and difficulty.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Streaming & Real-Time Rendering\n\n> Very common. Every AI-first company asks about this.\n\n### Core\n- How do you render incomplete Markdown mid-stream without layout thrash?\n- How do you throttle token appends so the DOM doesn't repaint 50×/sec?\n- How do you implement a stop-generation button that actually stops the stream?\n- What is the difference between SSE and WebSockets — when would you pick each?\n- How do you handle a stream that drops midway — reconnect, retry, or resume?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you buffer tokens before flushing to the DOM — what's the right interval?\n- How do you handle a code block that opens with ` ``` ` but the closing fence hasn't arrived yet?\n- How do you render a streaming table where rows arrive one token at a time?\n- How do you show a \"typing indicator\" that transitions seamlessly into real content?\n- How do you handle backpressure if the client is rendering slower than tokens arrive?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Conversation State Management\n\n> Very common. Core to any chat product.\n\n### Core\n- Where does conversation state live — client, server, or both?\n- How do you handle editing a previous message and regenerating from that point?\n- How do you implement branching conversations (retry gives a different response path)?\n- How do you sync conversation state across two open tabs on the same conversation?\n- What is your strategy when the context window fills up — truncate, summarize, or paginate?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you model a branched conversation as a data structure — tree vs linear array?\n- How do you reassemble the messages array after a mid-conversation edit?\n- How do you handle optimistic UI rollback if a regenerated message fails?\n- How do you implement \"undo\" for a sent message?\n- How do you persist draft messages across page refreshes?\n\n---\n\n## 3. MCP & Tool Use UI\n\n> Emerging hot topic. Most candidates haven't thought this through.\n\n### Core\n- How do you render a tool call pill — loading, success, and error states?\n- How does a confirm button in the UI map to the backend API call?\n- Why does `tool_result` go in as `role: \"user\"` in the Anthropic API?\n- How do you prevent a double-booking from a confirm button being clicked twice?\n- How do you communicate the trust boundary — data leaving Claude to a third-party MCP server?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you implement idempotency keys for destructive MCP actions like bookings or emails?\n- How do you render multi-step tool chains — 3 tool calls in one assistant turn?\n- How do you handle a tool call that times out after 30 seconds?\n- How do you diff the Anthropic vs OpenAI tool use protocol — `tool_use`/`tool_result` vs `tool_calls`/`tool` role?\n- How do you handle a partial tool result — MCP server returns incomplete data?\n- How do you show the user which external services were called and what data was shared?\n\n---\n\n## 4. Artifacts & Sandboxed Rendering\n\n> Common at companies building AI coding or document tools.\n\n### Core\n- How do you safely render Claude-generated HTML or React in the browser?\n- Why use an iframe sandbox — what attacks does it prevent?\n- How do you stream code into a live-reloading preview panel?\n- How does `postMessage` work between the host page and the sandboxed iframe?\n- How do you version artifacts — user edits vs Claude regenerates?\n\n### Deep\n- What CSP headers do you set on the sandboxed iframe and why?\n- How do you handle an artifact that imports an external CDN library — allow or block?\n- How do you diff two versions of an artifact and show a visual changelog?\n- How do you sync scroll position between the code editor and the rendered preview?\n- How do you handle an infinite loop inside a sandboxed React component?\n- How do you implement a \"revert to version N\" for an artifact?\n\n---\n\n## 5. Performance & Scalability\n\n> Senior-level signal. Shows production experience.\n\n### Core\n- How do you virtualize a conversation list with 500 messages?\n- How do you measure and optimize Time to First Token (TTFT)?\n- How do you lazy-load older conversation history as the user scrolls up?\n- How do you avoid re-rendering the entire message list on every new token?\n- How do you handle slow networks — skeleton states, progressive rendering?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you implement scroll anchoring so new tokens don't jump the viewport?\n- How do you calculate the dynamic height of a message before it has rendered (needed for virtualization)?\n- How do you debounce Markdown re-parsing during a fast token stream?\n- How do you measure token-per-second render rate on the client and alert on degradation?\n- How do you preload the next conversation in the sidebar so it feels instant?\n- What is your caching strategy for conversation history — memory, IndexedDB, server?\n\n---\n\n## 6. Auth, Security & Multitenancy\n\n> Senior-level. Differentiates engineers who've built multi-user systems.\n\n### Core\n- How do you scope conversations to a user — JWT claims, row-level security?\n- How do you implement org-level conversation isolation in a Team plan?\n- How do you prevent prompt injection through user-uploaded files?\n- How do you handle OAuth token refresh for MCP servers mid-conversation?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you invalidate all sessions for a user on password change without breaking active streams?\n- How do you implement conversation sharing with a public link — what's the permission model?\n- How do you audit-log every MCP action for enterprise compliance?\n- How do you prevent a malicious MCP server from exfiltrating conversation history?\n- How do you scope API keys so a developer key can't access another org's conversations?\n- How do you handle a user who belongs to multiple orgs — context switching mid-session?\n\n---\n\n## 7. Offline, Resilience & Error Handling\n\n> Differentiator. Shows you think beyond the happy path.\n\n### Core\n- What do you show if the SSE stream disconnects at token 200 of 800?\n- How do you queue a user message sent while offline and replay it on reconnect?\n- How do you distinguish a rate-limit error from a model error from a network error?\n- How do you implement exponential backoff on the SSE reconnect?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you implement a \"resume stream\" — continue generation from where it dropped?\n- How do you handle a partial message that was persisted to the DB mid-stream before disconnect?\n- How do you show a degraded-mode UI when the inference cluster is slow (p99 > 10s)?\n- What is your retry strategy for a failed MCP tool call — retry immediately, after delay, or ask user?\n- How do you surface rate limit information (e.g. requests remaining) to the user without alarming them?\n\n---\n\n## 8. Input & Multimodal UX\n\n> Common at companies with file upload, voice, or image features.\n\n### Core\n- How do you implement a textarea that grows with content but caps at a max height?\n- How do you handle large file uploads — chunking, progress, cancellation?\n- How do you render an image uploaded by the user inline in the conversation?\n- How do you implement slash commands (e.g. `/search`, `/summarize`) in the input box?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you implement voice input with live transcription feeding into the chat input?\n- How do you handle a PDF upload — extract text client-side or send the raw file?\n- How do you show a token count estimate for the current input before the user sends?\n- How do you implement drag-and-drop file attachment with paste-from-clipboard support?\n- How do you handle mixed multimodal input — image + text + file in one message?\n\n---\n\n## 9. API Design & Provider Abstraction\n\n> Relevant if building on top of multiple LLM providers.\n\n### Core\n- Why does Anthropic use strict alternating turns while OpenAI allows a `tool` role?\n- How do you normalize message history across Anthropic, OpenAI, and Gemini formats?\n- How do you handle provider-specific features (e.g. Anthropic extended thinking) without breaking abstraction?\n- What is the difference between `system` as a top-level field (Anthropic) vs a system message in the array (OpenAI)?\n\n### Deep\n- How do you build a provider-agnostic streaming adapter — same interface for SSE and WebSocket backends?\n- How do you handle model versioning — what happens when `claude-sonnet-4` is deprecated mid-product?\n- How do you implement automatic model fallback if the primary model returns a 529 overloaded error?\n- How do you estimate cost before sending a request — token counting per provider?\n\n---\n\n## 10. The \"Killer\" Questions\n\n> Questions that separate good candidates from great ones. Each forces multi-system thinking.\n\n1. **Edit message N in a 20-message conversation.** Forces you to think about branching history, context window re-assembly, optimistic UI rollback, and server-side state — all at once.\n\n2. **The confirm button is clicked twice in 200ms.** How do you guarantee exactly one booking? Covers button locking, idempotency keys, backend deduplication, and UX rollback.\n\n3. **The stream drops at token 400 of 1000.** What does the user see, what's in the DB, and how do you recover? Covers partial persistence, resume logic, and error UX.\n\n4. **Design the conversation sidebar for a user with 10,000 conversations.** Covers virtualization, search indexing, pagination, and optimistic rename/delete.\n\n5. **A Claude-generated React component has an infinite loop. How do you detect and handle it?** Covers sandboxing, timeout/heartbeat in the iframe, and graceful error rendering.\n\n6. **The MCP OAuth token expires mid-conversation during a multi-step agentic task.** Covers token refresh, mid-stream pause, user re-auth UX, and task resumption.\n\n---\n\n*Use the segmentation above to time-box your prep. Streaming + conversation state first, then MCP/artifacts, then the rest.*","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}}}
