{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Vw1vRCJxhceSipKPPdpaNs","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The file is saved at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-design-doc.md`.\n\nHere's what's in it:\n\n---\n\n**9 sections, 90+ questions total** — here's the breakdown:\n\n| # | Section | Core | Deep |\n|---|---------|------|------|\n| 1 | Checkout Flow & Form UX | 7 | 3 |\n| 2 | Payment Security & PCI Compliance | 7 | 3 |\n| 3 | State Management & Transaction Lifecycle | 7 | 3 |\n| 4 | Real-Time Updates & Webhooks | 7 | 3 |\n| 5 | Performance & Core Web Vitals | 7 | 3 |\n| 6 | Error Handling & Resilience | 7 | 3 |\n| 7 | Internationalization & Localization | 7 | 3 |\n| 8 | Observability & Analytics | 7 | 3 |\n| 9 | Architecture & Provider Abstraction | 7 | 3 |\n\n**Some of the sharpest questions in the bank:**\n\n- *\"What happens to a PaymentIntent if the user closes the tab during 3DS?\"* — forces the candidate to understand async payment state vs. UI lifecycle\n- *\"A pen tester says exposing the `client_secret` to the browser is a vulnerability. How do you evaluate that?\"* — tests PCI nuance vs. reflexive security panic\n- *\"Design a provider failover where Stripe 5xx → Adyen retry in <2s without the user noticing\"* — staff-level architecture + PSP-specific constraints\n- *\"Your success rate drops 7 points post-deploy — is it frontend or Stripe?\"* — diagnostic playbook under pressure\n- *\"Japan checkout: konbini payment, reversed address fields, no decimal yen\"* — tests whether i18n thinking is deep or surface-level"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: af9570d2231e491f2 (use SendMessage with to: 'af9570d2231e491f2' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 28563\ntool_uses: 2\nduration_ms: 179928</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f0c546b-796f-4811-b3ba-6d557f88a795","uuid":"7feb4489-7dce-4f61-928d-76c527eb967d","timestamp":"2026-06-20T18:28:19.157Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write a comprehensive frontend system design interview question bank for a **payments system** (think Stripe, Braintree, PayPal, or similar — a checkout + payment processing frontend).\n\nSave it to: `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-design-doc.md`\n\n## Structure to follow\nMatch this exact format from the Claude reference doc:\n\n```\n# Payments System Frontend System Design — Interview Questions\n\nA comprehensive reference of deep questions across all segments, organized by theme and difficulty.\n\n---\n\n## 1. <Section Title>\n\n> <One-line note on frequency/importance>\n\n### Core\n- Question 1\n- Question 2\n- ... (5+ questions)\n\n### Deep\n- Question 1\n- ... (3+ questions)\n\n---\n\n## 2. <Section Title>\n...\n```\n\n## Sections to cover (6–10 total)\n\nDesign sections around these themes for a payments frontend:\n\n1. **Checkout Flow & Form UX** — multi-step checkout, card input, address forms, error handling\n2. **Payment Security & PCI Compliance** — tokenization, iframes (Stripe Elements), CSP, sandboxing, sensitive data isolation\n3. **State Management & Transaction Lifecycle** — payment intent state machine, optimistic UI, idempotency, retries\n4. **Real-Time Updates & Webhooks** — webhook-driven status updates, polling vs WebSocket vs SSE for payment confirmations\n5. **Performance & Core Web Vitals** — checkout page load, bundle splitting, lazy loading payment SDK, CLS from card iframe injection\n6. **Error Handling & Resilience** — network failures, card declines, 3DS challenges, retry strategies, graceful degradation\n7. **Internationalization & Localization** — currency formatting, RTL support, local payment methods, tax/VAT display\n8. **Observability & Analytics** — funnel tracking, drop-off detection, error monitoring, payment success rate dashboards\n9. (optional) **Architecture & Provider Abstraction** — multi-PSP routing, Stripe vs Adyen vs Braintree abstraction layer\n\n## Quality bar\n- Every section needs 5+ Core questions and 3+ Deep questions\n- Questions should be interview-depth: specific enough to have a real answer, not generic\n- Include domain-specific nuance (e.g. \"How does Stripe Elements prevent your page from ever touching raw card data?\", \"What happens to the payment intent if the user closes the tab during 3DS?\")\n- Match the tone and depth of the Claude reference doc provided above\n\nWrite the full file now. Do not truncate.","agentId":"af9570d2231e491f2","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The file is saved at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-design-doc.md`.\n\nHere's what's in it:\n\n---\n\n**9 sections, 90+ questions total** — here's the breakdown:\n\n| # | Section | Core | Deep |\n|---|---------|------|------|\n| 1 | Checkout Flow & Form UX | 7 | 3 |\n| 2 | Payment Security & PCI Compliance | 7 | 3 |\n| 3 | State Management & Transaction Lifecycle | 7 | 3 |\n| 4 | Real-Time Updates & Webhooks | 7 | 3 |\n| 5 | Performance & Core Web Vitals | 7 | 3 |\n| 6 | Error Handling & Resilience | 7 | 3 |\n| 7 | Internationalization & Localization | 7 | 3 |\n| 8 | Observability & Analytics | 7 | 3 |\n| 9 | Architecture & Provider Abstraction | 7 | 3 |\n\n**Some of the sharpest questions in the bank:**\n\n- *\"What happens to a PaymentIntent if the user closes the tab during 3DS?\"* — forces the candidate to understand async payment state vs. UI lifecycle\n- *\"A pen tester says exposing the `client_secret` to the browser is a vulnerability. How do you evaluate that?\"* — tests PCI nuance vs. reflexive security panic\n- *\"Design a provider failover where Stripe 5xx → Adyen retry in <2s without the user noticing\"* — staff-level architecture + PSP-specific constraints\n- *\"Your success rate drops 7 points post-deploy — is it frontend or Stripe?\"* — diagnostic playbook under pressure\n- *\"Japan checkout: konbini payment, reversed address fields, no decimal yen\"* — tests whether i18n thinking is deep or surface-level"}],"resolvedModel":"blackboxai/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5","totalDurationMs":179928,"totalTokens":28563,"totalToolUseCount":2,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6811,"cache_read_input_tokens":21266,"output_tokens":485,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6811},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":206,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
